      },
      "eyebrow": "Learn",
      "title": "Read the evidence, not the shortcut",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Review the two authorized operations against the same state. The first holds the lock; the competing operation must fail lock acquisition and leave state unchanged. Retain the .tflock observations and contention evidence. Keep this coordination test separate from authorization tests for direct state-object access.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "terraform.state_locking"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "terraform.state_locking#f1",
              "terraform.state_locking#f2",
              "terraform.state_locking#f3",
              "terraform.state_locking#f4"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "terraform.state_locking#tb4"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Force-unlock has a narrow recovery role: a failed operation left a lock and automatic unlocking failed. It is not a safe bypass for another active writer. Lock-file locking remains opt-in and is not an authorization boundary; disabling it to let the second operation proceed defeats the contention test.",
          "role": "misconception",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "terraform.state_locking"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "terraform.state_locking#m1",
              "terraform.state_locking#f1",
              "terraform.state_locking#f4"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "terraform.state_locking#tb5",
              "terraform.state_locking#tb6"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
